A||||15||making it better||need turbo info ||||1||
Z||000000||making it better||04-03-2000||02:07 AM||||planning to do engine work in future, but want to add a turbo for now.  Want to know if a turbo from a 3.8 would be to much for now. I have a 2.8 ||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||04-03-2000||06:35 AM||||First off, have a grain of salt as I am not a turbo expert. I do have a turbo car (NOT my Fiero unfortunately) so I guess I am quasi qualified. Firstly, any turbo you add will require lots of custom engineering- not the cheapest path to walk. A performance rebuild will cost you less then a prepackaged turbo kit from Design 1 for example<BR>Secondly, Buick turbos are pretty big, giving huge boost but also big LAG when hooked up to the little 2.8.<BR>Thirdly, Buick turbos are pretty expensive and low in production compared to T-Bird turbo coupes. My suggestion would be go that route and take good notes then tell me how to do it. Good luck! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87PegasusGT||04-03-2000||03:29 PM||||You may want to consider what I am doing. 3.4 is cheaper than a turbo,and is almost no mod. You can turbo that also while still keeping stock appearance.||||reg||1
Z||000003||N_Man||04-03-2000||08:12 PM||||if possible try dropping the 3.8 turbo <BR>I have no clue what it would take but my guess is that its easier than doing all the mods to the 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||04-03-2000||09:48 PM||||Are you saying it would be easier to swap a GN motor w/ turbo than adapting a smaller T-3 to a 2.8?  I wouldn't know cause I haven't done either, but the turbo 2.8 atleast sounds possible.  I've never even heard of a 3.8 turbo Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||04-03-2000||11:02 PM||||I have to agree with Stimpy here... There's ALOT of fabrication to be done here if you're serious about it.  I think some people get the impression that a turbo is like a bolt-on modification or something.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||04-03-2000||11:22 PM||||I think, if you don't go too wild with boost, a turbo is pretty much a bolt-on(besides the fabrication of pipes and such). Nothing <B>has</B> to be done to the motor with mild boost. But, as always, I could be wrong. <P>After much researching I have decided to turbo my 2.8. If it blows the bottom end out of the engine, I will rebuild it stronger. If it's beyond repair I will save up to get a new 3.4 block. If it explodes and I am still able to walk I will get another Fiero and start over. If it kills me I will be in heavan (hopefully heavan) searching for a Fiero and a turbo  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>This is what I have so far.  <A HREF="http://msnhomepages.talkcity.com/RallyRd/scca_fiero/Turbo_project.html" TARGET=_blank>http://msnhomepages.talkcity.com/RallyRd/scca_fiero/Turbo_project.html</A> <BR>These items and more and more knowledge every day. I ordered a book call <B>Maximum Boost</B> to help me on my quest. I have been getting sidetracked from this project, but eventually will get it done. I am going to do this!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||turbo86se||04-04-2000||12:22 AM||||Hey SCCA- your wait is over! Hop on a plane to SC and I'll let you drive a turbo-charged Fiero first-hand! Maybe $15K would talk me out of it! Naaaa! I'd cry for a week!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=226077&a=1676370" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=226077&a=1676370</A> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||04-04-2000||12:51 AM||||$15,000?? Will you take payments?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000009||terryk||04-04-2000||01:02 AM||||I think you will suck a piston or blow a head gasket before the bottom end gives out.<P>Remember, you need a cheap fuse in the engine. The head gasket is the best fuse. The labor and gasket is cheaper than replacing valves and pistons.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dan86gt3.8||04-04-2000||03:30 AM||||Yall all know I am very interseted in this subject!!!!!  So let me know if you figure something out.  I think someone has said that it has ben done before.  They didn't say who or where, though.  The best thing I can think of is get a 3.8 beef up the bottom end, maybe do some head work and ethier have a turbo sho fab you a turbo for it, or design your own.  Anywyas I am always intrested in the gn/series II turbo engines!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000011||RobertVol||04-04-2000||10:35 AM||||Speaking of the design one system. has anybody have one on their car ? if so what is like. I was interested in doing this.||||reg||1
Z||000012||87PegasusGT||04-04-2000||01:14 PM||||Maximum boost is an EXCELLENT book. I read it already. I am also reading abook on NOS installation right now.||||reg||1
Z||000013||SCCA FIERO||04-04-2000||04:35 PM||||RobertVol, here is a webpage of a guy that has the stage 2 Design One system. It looks very nice and for $4,000 it better!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.trix.com/fiero/turbo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.trix.com/fiero/turbo/index.html</A> <P>Here is where I got the idea to do my project. Dennis is well known for his beast and I think most everyone knows his site. If not here it is  <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/dlagrua/turbo.htm</A> <P>And then there is this guy with a 3.1 turbo in his Z24 making about 450hp (WOW!!) <BR> <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/TurboZ24/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/TurboZ24/</A> ||||reg||1
